{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-261018-f583915aea8ff7c002895c81","sequence":5,"timestamp":"2026-10-18T12:50:43.830703Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"f6fd491f-270c-4625-b0d2-29aa04633ed6"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"BUG-261018-ukk6c8","element_type":"bug"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-261018-435a89c4c71049a3f44aa9ad","causal_order":1,"operation":"progress","changes":[{"field":"notes","before":{"kind":"text","text":""},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Root cause (2026-10-18): not the firewall. The Go race runtime sleeps atexit_sleep_ms=1000 before exit; a trivial -race binary takes 1.0s, 0.01s with GORACE=atexit_sleep_ms=0. Both tests re-exec the race test binary as fake commands, so each helper costs +1s and overruns their budgets. Fix: helper envs carry GORACE=atexit_sleep_ms=0 (test-only). Race lane on maccore green after the fix; red before (race-main-01.log). Why it passed on 2026-10-17 is unexplained."}}]}
